Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: When are representations and warranties required to be made according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: At Closing Only\nOption B: At Signing & At Closing\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 8.4 Conditions to Obligations of Acquirer and Merger Sub to Complete the Merger. The obligations of Acquirer and Merger Sub to complete the Merger are subject to the satisfaction, or waiver by Acquirer, at or prior to the Closing Date of the following conditions: (a) the representations and warranties of the Target Company contained in this Agreement, disregarding any qualifications as to materiality or Company Material Adverse Effect, shall be true and correct as of the Closing Date, except for those representations and warranties that are expressly made as of a specific date, which shall be true and correct as of such date; (b) notwithstanding the foregoing, if the representations and warranties of the Target Company are not true and correct as of the date of this Agreement, the Acquirer may still proceed with the Merger if the inaccuracies do not result in a Company Material Adverse Effect as of the Closing Date; (c) any exceptions to these representations and warranties must be disclosed in writing by the Target Company at least five business days prior to the Closing Date. (Page 82)
