Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: When are representations and warranties required to be made according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: At Closing Only\nOption B: At Signing & At Closing\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 9.3 Conditions to Obligations of Parent to Effect the Merger. The obligations of Parent to effect the Merger are subject to the satisfaction or waiver by Parent of the following conditions: (a) The representations and warranties of the Company set forth in this Agreement shall be true and correct as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date, with the same force and effect as if made on and as of such dates, except where the failure to be so true and correct would not, individually or in the aggregate, have a Material Adverse Effect; (b) notwithstanding the foregoing, the representations and warranties that are qualified by materiality shall be true and correct in all respects as of the date hereof and as of the Closing Date; (c) representations and warranties made as of a specific date need only be true and correct as of such specific date. (Page 55)\nAnswer:
